# Ed-Fi API v8 pilot kit: the baseline education organization hierarchy (Task 14, FR-EDORG-1, 3, 6,
# 9, 10, 16). `init/bootstrap.sh` (Task 10) already creates these five records automatically on
# startup (FR-EDORG-12) -- you do not need to run this file for a normal start. It exists for two
# other reasons: to show exactly what the kit created on your behalf, and to add or repair
# organizations by hand. bootstrap/baseline-edorgs.json is the single source of truth for the
# identifiers, grade levels, and school categories below; this file and that one must never diverge
# (FR-EDORG-14) -- see bootstrap/README.md.
#
# Fill in @key and @secret before running anything past the token request, from
# .runtime/bootstrap-credentials.json or a REST Client environment -- see http/smoke.http's header
# for both options. This file is intended for the bootstrap (ADMIN) credential specifically
# (FR-EDORG-11): only it is broad enough to create education organizations. Running these requests
# with a scoped participant integration credential instead is the most likely failure (FR-EDORG-13)
# and returns 403, for example:
#   "No relationships have been established between the caller's education organization id claim(s)
#   ('<your scoped id>') and the resource item's 'StateEducationAgencyId' value."
#
# Every POST below is safe to re-run, including against an environment where bootstrapping already
# created the baseline: DMS upserts by natural key, so a repeat POST returns 200, not a duplicate
# (FR-EDORG-6).

@baseUrl = https://localhost/api
@key =
@secret =

# Baseline identifiers (bootstrap/baseline-edorgs.json, FR-EDORG-7). Chosen not to collide with the
# populated template's sample organizations -- LEA 255901, ESC 255950, post-secondary institution
# 6000203, community provider 19255901, and their schools (FR-EDORG-8).
@seaId = 99
@leaId = 9900
@elementarySchoolId = 990001
@middleSchoolId = 990002
@highSchoolId = 990003

### Token
# @name token
POST {{baseUrl}}/oauth/token
Authorization: Basic {{key}} {{secret}}
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=client_credentials

# -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The hierarchy, in dependency order (FR-EDORG-3): the SEA first, since nothing references it;
# then the LEA, which references the SEA; then the three schools, which reference the LEA.
# -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

### 1. State Education Agency
POST {{baseUrl}}/data/ed-fi/stateEducationAgencies
Authorization: Bearer {{token.response.body.access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "stateEducationAgencyId": {{seaId}},
  "nameOfInstitution": "Pilot Kit State Education Agency",
  "categories": [
    { "educationOrganizationCategoryDescriptor": "uri://ed-fi.org/EducationOrganizationCategoryDescriptor#State Education Agency" }
  ]
}

### 2. Local Education Agency, referencing the SEA above
POST {{baseUrl}}/data/ed-fi/localEducationAgencies
Authorization: Bearer {{token.response.body.access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "localEducationAgencyId": {{leaId}},
  "nameOfInstitution": "Pilot Kit Local Education Agency",
  "localEducationAgencyCategoryDescriptor": "uri://ed-fi.org/LocalEducationAgencyCategoryDescriptor#Regular public school district",
  "categories": [
    { "educationOrganizationCategoryDescriptor": "uri://ed-fi.org/EducationOrganizationCategoryDescriptor#Local Education Agency" }
  ],
  "stateEducationAgencyReference": { "stateEducationAgencyId": {{seaId}} }
}

### 3. Elementary school, referencing the LEA above.
# DS 5.2 naming quirk (bootstrap/README.md): schools use "educationOrganizationCategories", not
# "categories" like the SEA/LEA above -- DMS rejects the wrong name with 400 "categories is required".
POST {{baseUrl}}/data/ed-fi/schools
Authorization: Bearer {{token.response.body.access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "schoolId": {{elementarySchoolId}},
  "nameOfInstitution": "Pilot Kit Elementary School",
  "educationOrganizationCategories": [
    { "educationOrganizationCategoryDescriptor": "uri://ed-fi.org/EducationOrganizationCategoryDescriptor#School" }
  ],
  "schoolCategories": [
    { "schoolCategoryDescriptor": "uri://ed-fi.org/SchoolCategoryDescriptor#Elementary School" }
  ],
  "gradeLevels": [
    { "gradeLevelDescriptor": "uri://ed-fi.org/GradeLevelDescriptor#Kindergarten" },
    { "gradeLevelDescriptor": "uri://ed-fi.org/GradeLevelDescriptor#First grade" },
    { "gradeLevelDescriptor": "uri://ed-fi.org/GradeLevelDescriptor#Second grade" },
    { "gradeLevelDescriptor": "uri://ed-fi.org/GradeLevelDescriptor#Third grade" },
    { "gradeLevelDescriptor": "uri://ed-fi.org/GradeLevelDescriptor#Fourth grade" },
    { "gradeLevelDescriptor": "uri://ed-fi.org/GradeLevelDescriptor#Fifth grade" }
  ],
  "localEducationAgencyReference": { "localEducationAgencyId": {{leaId}} }
}

### 4. Middle school, referencing the LEA above
POST {{baseUrl}}/data/ed-fi/schools
Authorization: Bearer {{token.response.body.access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "schoolId": {{middleSchoolId}},
  "nameOfInstitution": "Pilot Kit Middle School",
  "educationOrganizationCategories": [
    { "educationOrganizationCategoryDescriptor": "uri://ed-fi.org/EducationOrganizationCategoryDescriptor#School" }
  ],
  "schoolCategories": [
    { "schoolCategoryDescriptor": "uri://ed-fi.org/SchoolCategoryDescriptor#Middle School" }
  ],
  "gradeLevels": [
    { "gradeLevelDescriptor": "uri://ed-fi.org/GradeLevelDescriptor#Sixth grade" },
    { "gradeLevelDescriptor": "uri://ed-fi.org/GradeLevelDescriptor#Seventh grade" },
    { "gradeLevelDescriptor": "uri://ed-fi.org/GradeLevelDescriptor#Eighth grade" }
  ],
  "localEducationAgencyReference": { "localEducationAgencyId": {{leaId}} }
}

### 5. High school, referencing the LEA above
POST {{baseUrl}}/data/ed-fi/schools
Authorization: Bearer {{token.response.body.access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "schoolId": {{highSchoolId}},
  "nameOfInstitution": "Pilot Kit High School",
  "educationOrganizationCategories": [
    { "educationOrganizationCategoryDescriptor": "uri://ed-fi.org/EducationOrganizationCategoryDescriptor#School" }
  ],
  "schoolCategories": [
    { "schoolCategoryDescriptor": "uri://ed-fi.org/SchoolCategoryDescriptor#High School" }
  ],
  "gradeLevels": [
    { "gradeLevelDescriptor": "uri://ed-fi.org/GradeLevelDescriptor#Ninth grade" },
    { "gradeLevelDescriptor": "uri://ed-fi.org/GradeLevelDescriptor#Tenth grade" },
    { "gradeLevelDescriptor": "uri://ed-fi.org/GradeLevelDescriptor#Eleventh grade" },
    { "gradeLevelDescriptor": "uri://ed-fi.org/GradeLevelDescriptor#Twelfth grade" }
  ],
  "localEducationAgencyReference": { "localEducationAgencyId": {{leaId}} }
}

# -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Verification (FR-EDORG-9): read the hierarchy back by reference, rather than by the ids you just
# posted, so you can confirm the relationships resolved and not only that each record exists.
# -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

### Verify: the LEA, by its SEA reference
GET {{baseUrl}}/data/ed-fi/localEducationAgencies?stateEducationAgencyId={{seaId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token.response.body.access_token}}

### Verify: the three schools, by their LEA reference
GET {{baseUrl}}/data/ed-fi/schools?localEducationAgencyId={{leaId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token.response.body.access_token}}

# -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Templates for adding more organizations (FR-EDORG-16). Copy a block below, uncomment it (remove the
# leading "# " from every line, including the JSON), and change the id and name. Pick an id that
# doesn't collide with the baseline above or the populated template's sample organizations
# (255901, 255950, 6000203, 19255901, and their schools -- FR-EDORG-8). Keep every reference target
# earlier in the file than the record that references it (FR-EDORG-3), and add the new record to
# bootstrap/baseline-edorgs.json too if it should also be created automatically on startup
# (FR-EDORG-14).
# -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

